Pre-Phase F hardening - transfer ownership and stack measurement
Waveshare ESP32-S3-LCD-2.8 (SKU 30223, non-touch) - 2026-08-04

Captured from the native USB Serial/JTAG console at 115200 baud.
Firmware: hardware-validation profile, uncommitted hardening batch.

Normalisation applied to this file, and nothing else:
  - ANSI colour escapes removed
  - CR removed and trailing whitespace stripped, so the file is LF-only
  - ESP-IDF Verbose-level lines (prefix 'V') dropped: SPI bus-lock and
    polling-transaction plumbing, hundreds of lines per frame.
    Debug, Info, Warning and Error levels kept in full.

No device MAC address, serial number, host path or username appears here.

Key fields:
  transfers submitted=/completed= must always be equal
  peak_in_flight=1 is the buffer-safety proof: only one transfer is ever
    outstanding, so the shared band buffer is never rewritten under DMA.
    Before this change up to 6 could be queued against the same buffer.
  spurious= and wait_timeouts= must always be 0
  free_low_bytes= is the FreeRTOS high-water mark, in BYTES on ESP-IDF

==============================================================================
PART 1 - pattern cycle at 4096-byte prd_button_val (pre-change measurement)
All 9 static patterns: corner markers, colour bars, 1px checkerboard,
gradient, black, white, near-black, orange, comparison chart.
